   "prompt": "<p>Build a tiny roofline calculator for a made-up GPU (100 TFLOP/s, 2 TB/s). For each op compute FLOPs, bytes moved (bf16, 2 bytes per element), arithmetic intensity, whether it is compute- or memory-bound, and the roofline minimum time. Then count transformer FLOPs per token per layer for <code>d = 768, T = 1024</code>, and estimate training time for a 12-layer model on 10B tokens at 40% MFU with <code>C = 6ND</code>.</p><p>Expected output:</p><pre><code>ridge point: 50 FLOP/byte\nmatmul 4096x4096x4096  AI  1365.3  compute  min   1374.4 us\nmatmul 16x4096x4096    AI    15.9  memory   min     16.9 us\nmatvec 1x4096x4096     AI     1.0  memory   min     16.8 us\ngelu 8192x4096         AI     2.0  memory   min     67.1 us\nfwd FLOPs/token/layer: 17.3 M\nN = 84.9 M, train FLOPs = 5.10e+18, 35.4 h at 40% MFU</code></pre>",
   "starter": "PEAK = 100e12   # FLOP/s, bf16 dense (made-up round-number GPU)\nBW = 2e12       # bytes/s of HBM bandwidth\nridge = PEAK / BW\nprint(f\"ridge point: {ridge:.0f} FLOP/byte\")\n\ndef matmul(m, k, n, bytes_per=2):\n    # TODO: FLOPs of (m x k) @ (k x n), and bytes for reading A, B and writing C\n    flops = moved = 1\n    return flops, moved\n\ndef elementwise(numel, flops_per, bytes_per=2):\n    # TODO: flops_per FLOPs per element; read every element once and write once\n    return 1, 1\n\nops = [\n    (\"matmul 4096x4096x4096\", *matmul(4096, 4096, 4096)),\n    (\"matmul 16x4096x4096\", *matmul(16, 4096, 4096)),\n    (\"matvec 1x4096x4096\", *matmul(1, 4096, 4096)),\n    (\"gelu 8192x4096\", *elementwise(8192 * 4096, 8)),\n]\nfor name, f, b in ops:\n    ai = f / b\n    t = 0.0        # TODO: roofline lower bound = slower of compute time and memory time\n    bound = \"?\"    # TODO: \"compute\" if ai >= ridge else \"memory\"\n    print(f\"{name:22s} AI {ai:7.1f}  {bound:7s}  min {t * 1e6:8.1f} us\")\n\nd, T, layers = 768, 1024, 12\nper_tok_layer = 0  # TODO: 24*d^2 (projections + MLP) + 4*T*d (QK^T and AV)\nprint(f\"fwd FLOPs/token/layer: {per_tok_layer / 1e6:.1f} M\")\nN = 12 * layers * d * d          # non-embedding parameters\nD = 10e9                         # training tokens\nC = 0                            # TODO: 6 N D\nhours = C / (PEAK * 0.40) / 3600\nprint(f\"N = {N / 1e6:.1f} M, train FLOPs = {C:.2e}, {hours:.1f} h at 40% MFU\")\n",
   "solution": "PEAK = 100e12   # FLOP/s, bf16 dense (made-up round-number GPU)\nBW = 2e12       # bytes/s of HBM bandwidth\nridge = PEAK / BW\nprint(f\"ridge point: {ridge:.0f} FLOP/byte\")\n\ndef matmul(m, k, n, bytes_per=2):\n    flops = 2 * m * k * n                        # one multiply + one add per term\n    moved = bytes_per * (m * k + k * n + m * n)  # read A, read B, write C\n    return flops, moved\n\ndef elementwise(numel, flops_per, bytes_per=2):\n    return flops_per * numel, 2 * bytes_per * numel   # read x, write y\n\nops = [\n    (\"matmul 4096x4096x4096\", *matmul(4096, 4096, 4096)),\n    (\"matmul 16x4096x4096\", *matmul(16, 4096, 4096)),\n    (\"matvec 1x4096x4096\", *matmul(1, 4096, 4096)),\n    (\"gelu 8192x4096\", *elementwise(8192 * 4096, 8)),\n]\nfor name, f, b in ops:\n    ai = f / b\n    t = max(f / PEAK, b / BW)\n    bound = \"compute\" if ai >= ridge else \"memory\"\n    print(f\"{name:22s} AI {ai:7.1f}  {bound:7s}  min {t * 1e6:8.1f} us\")\n\nd, T, layers = 768, 1024, 12\nper_tok_layer = 24 * d * d + 4 * T * d\nprint(f\"fwd FLOPs/token/layer: {per_tok_layer / 1e6:.1f} M\")\nN = 12 * layers * d * d\nD = 10e9\nC = 6 * N * D\nhours = C / (PEAK * 0.40) / 3600\nprint(f\"N = {N / 1e6:.1f} M, train FLOPs = {C:.2e}, {hours:.1f} h at 40% MFU\")\n",
   "expected": "ridge point: 50 FLOP/byte\nmatmul 4096x4096x4096  AI  1365.3  compute  min   1374.4 us\nmatmul 16x4096x4096    AI    15.9  memory   min     16.9 us\nmatvec 1x4096x4096     AI     1.0  memory   min     16.8 us\ngelu 8192x4096         AI     2.0  memory   min     67.1 us\nfwd FLOPs/token/layer: 17.3 M\nN = 84.9 M, train FLOPs = 5.10e+18, 35.4 h at 40% MFU",
