   "prompt": "<p>Two architecture calculations. (1) KV-cache bytes per token and per 32K-token sequence for MHA, GQA-8, MQA and MLA (latent 512 + RoPE key 64), with 32 layers, head_dim 128, bf16. (2) A mixture-of-experts layer with 8 experts (<code>d = 512, d_ff = 2048</code>) and top-2 routing: total vs active parameters. Then route 8 tokens over 4 experts with the given router logits: print each token's top-2 experts and renormalised gates, the load per expert, and the Switch load-balancing loss <code>E · Σ f·P</code>.</p><p>Expected output:</p><pre><code>MHA 32 kv heads     512 KiB/token  16.000 GiB at 32K\nGQA 8 kv heads      128 KiB/token   4.000 GiB at 32K\nMQA 1 kv head        16 KiB/token   0.500 GiB at 32K\nMLA latent 512+64    36 KiB/token   1.125 GiB at 32K\nMoE total 16.78 M, active 4.20 M (25%)\ntoken 0: experts [0, 1] gates 0.731 0.269\ntoken 1: experts [1, 0] gates 0.846 0.154\ntoken 2: experts [0, 1] gates 0.525 0.475\ntoken 3: experts [2, 3] gates 0.646 0.354\ntoken 4: experts [0, 3] gates 0.750 0.250\ntoken 5: experts [0, 1] gates 0.711 0.289\ntoken 6: experts [1, 2] gates 0.525 0.475\ntoken 7: experts [0, 2] gates 0.786 0.214\nload per expert: [6, 5, 3, 2]\nbalance loss 1.155 (1.000 = perfectly balanced)</code></pre>",
   "starter": "import numpy as np\nGiB = 2**30\nLyr, H, hd, ctx, B2 = 32, 32, 128, 32768, 2     # B2 = bytes per value (bf16)\ndef kv(heads):\n    return 1   # TODO: K and V, every layer, `heads` KV heads of size hd\nmla = 1        # TODO: MLA caches one latent of 512 + a 64-dim RoPE key per layer\nfor name, per in ((\"MHA 32 kv heads\", kv(32)), (\"GQA 8 kv heads\", kv(8)),\n                  (\"MQA 1 kv head\", kv(1)), (\"MLA latent 512+64\", mla)):\n    print(f\"{name:18s} {per // 1024:4d} KiB/token  {per * ctx / GiB:6.3f} GiB at 32K\")\n\nd, dff, E, k = 512, 2048, 8, 2\nexpert = 2 * d * dff             # one MLP: up and down projections, no bias\ntotal = 1                        # TODO: all experts + router (d x E)\nactive = 1                       # TODO: k experts + router\nprint(f\"MoE total {total / 1e6:.2f} M, active {active / 1e6:.2f} M ({100 * active / total:.0f}%)\")\n\nlogits = np.array([[2.0, 1.0, 0.1, -1.0], [0.5, 2.2, 0.3, 0.0],\n                   [1.5, 1.4, -0.5, 0.2], [0.1, 0.2, 2.5, 1.9],\n                   [2.1, -0.3, 0.4, 1.0], [1.8, 0.9, 0.0, -0.2],\n                   [0.3, 1.7, 1.6, 0.1], [2.4, 0.2, 1.1, 0.5]])   # 8 tokens x 4 experts\nnE = logits.shape[1]\nprobs = np.ones_like(logits) / nE   # TODO: row-wise softmax of the router logits\ntop = np.zeros((len(logits), 2), dtype=int)   # TODO: indices of the 2 largest logits per row\nload = np.zeros(nE)\nfor t in range(len(logits)):\n    sel = probs[t, top[t]]\n    gates = sel / sel.sum()         # renormalise over the 2 chosen experts\n    # TODO: count one assignment for each chosen expert in load\n    print(f\"token {t}: experts {[int(e) for e in top[t]]} gates {gates[0]:.3f} {gates[1]:.3f}\")\nf = load / max(load.sum(), 1)       # fraction of assignments per expert\nP = probs.mean(0)                   # mean router probability per expert\nprint(\"load per expert:\", [int(x) for x in load])\nprint(f\"balance loss {nE * float(np.sum(f * P)):.3f} (1.000 = perfectly balanced)\")\n",
   "solution": "import numpy as np\nGiB = 2**30\nLyr, H, hd, ctx, B2 = 32, 32, 128, 32768, 2\ndef kv(heads):\n    return 2 * Lyr * heads * hd * B2\nmla = Lyr * (512 + 64) * B2\nfor name, per in ((\"MHA 32 kv heads\", kv(32)), (\"GQA 8 kv heads\", kv(8)),\n                  (\"MQA 1 kv head\", kv(1)), (\"MLA latent 512+64\", mla)):\n    print(f\"{name:18s} {per // 1024:4d} KiB/token  {per * ctx / GiB:6.3f} GiB at 32K\")\n\nd, dff, E, k = 512, 2048, 8, 2\nexpert = 2 * d * dff\ntotal = E * expert + d * E\nactive = k * expert + d * E\nprint(f\"MoE total {total / 1e6:.2f} M, active {active / 1e6:.2f} M ({100 * active / total:.0f}%)\")\n\nlogits = np.array([[2.0, 1.0, 0.1, -1.0], [0.5, 2.2, 0.3, 0.0],\n                   [1.5, 1.4, -0.5, 0.2], [0.1, 0.2, 2.5, 1.9],\n                   [2.1, -0.3, 0.4, 1.0], [1.8, 0.9, 0.0, -0.2],\n                   [0.3, 1.7, 1.6, 0.1], [2.4, 0.2, 1.1, 0.5]])\nnE = logits.shape[1]\nprobs = np.exp(logits - logits.max(1, keepdims=True))\nprobs /= probs.sum(1, keepdims=True)\ntop = np.argsort(-logits, axis=1)[:, :2]\nload = np.zeros(nE)\nfor t in range(len(logits)):\n    sel = probs[t, top[t]]\n    gates = sel / sel.sum()\n    load[top[t]] += 1\n    print(f\"token {t}: experts {[int(e) for e in top[t]]} gates {gates[0]:.3f} {gates[1]:.3f}\")\nf = load / load.sum()\nP = probs.mean(0)\nprint(\"load per expert:\", [int(x) for x in load])\nprint(f\"balance loss {nE * float(np.sum(f * P)):.3f} (1.000 = perfectly balanced)\")\n",
